> BTW WTF is moonmist?

A mystery game similar to Adventure (if you're familiar
with that), but takes place in a (ostensibly haunted)
mansion, instead of in a cave system.  It's from Infocom.
It's a "pure text based" game.  (Imagine writing a game
that gets input only from keywords typed on a keyboard,
and gives output only from the printf() function.
You get the idea.)  Like Nethack, thinking before each
move is important.  Even more so, because you only get
a limited number of moves.  Each move is "1 minute" in
game time, and you only get from 6PM to 6AM to solve
the crime.  If you haven't solved it by sunrise, you
loose.

Hint: when the intercom at the gate asks you for your
favorite color, answering "red", "blue", "green", or
"yellow" will give 4 completely different versions of
the mystery.

Googling:

   Infocom Moonmist

gives 12,300 hits.  Lots of info and links.  Download
it and play it and see what you think.

> Is it any good?

As with most things, "good" here is in the eye of the
beholder; but in my opinion, yes.

